<title>UK: UK'S RANK SAYS BUYS BACK 41 MLN SHARES.</title>
<headline>UK'S RANK SAYS BUYS BACK 41 MLN SHARES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>British leisure company Rank Group Plc said on Friday it had bought back 41.428 million shares, representing 4.9 percent of its current issued capital, at 3.45 stg each.  </p>
<p>Rank said it had bought the shares from BZW Securities and NatWest Securities.</p>
<p>Earlier on Friday, Rank confirmed it would start to buy back up to 83.6 million shares, around 10 percent of its issued share capital.</p>
<p>Rank's share price had risen to a high of 368 pence during the day and was 7-1/2 pence up at 347 1/2p at 1515 GMT.</p>
<p>---London Newsroom +44 171 542 4366</p>
